# Pricing unknown ground (#18) was the first change of the step COST rather than of sources, and it gave the best untuned score (27.7, holdout 29.0); the body (radius 0.45) also pays for walls it walks beside, scraping, sliding and clipping corners, which the wave ignores (the tuner drove the diagonal discount of #4 down to 0.75, a hint that cutting corners near walls costs). Adding a CLEARANCE cost (each step discounted by the number of solid cells around it) makes plans keep to open floor and the middles of corridors, so walks get faster and fewer end in a slide or a press.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel scent
channel bad
channel here
channel value
channel dark
channel injection
channel wave
channel trail

rule track:
  when 1
  set trail = max(here, 0.97 * trail)

rule darkness:
  when 1
  set dark = 0.5 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid) + 0.5 * avg8(dark)

rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(where(scent + thing < 0.05, 0, source), thing * (1 - bad), where(scent + thing < 0.05, source, 0) * (0.3 + 2.0 * dark)) / (1 + 0.5 * sum8(solid))

# a step costs more on unknown ground (may be wall) and beside walls (the body scrapes and slides there)
rule plan:
  when 1
  set wave = max(injection, (1 - 0.08 * (1 - free)) * (1 - 0.02 * sum8(solid)) * max(0.94 * max4(wave), 0.916214 * max8(wave))) * (1 - solid * (1 - leak))

rule read:
  when 1
  set value = wave * (1 - 0.4 * trail)
